  "method": "Sampled while the measurements ran, by a sampler outside the project: CPU load over all logical processors every 5 s (the measurement itself included; \"before\" is the 10 s idle window ahead of each step), free physical memory every 5 s, and the power source (BatteryStatus.PowerOnline) and battery charge every 60 s and at each step change. A sample belongs to the step whose start and end contain it; two steps that waited for the measurement limiter start when it let them run, so they have no idle window before them. The sanity suites are not listed: they are w5-fix's final Windows runs on the same build digest (reused). The 2.7.0 side of the matrix ran partly under outside load (about 07:42–08:04: CPU at 99 % for minutes, free memory down to 3.2 GB; not part of this project); the 6 rows measured then were run again alone (the next step), and those reruns replace them. The first run of external pair 1 is listed although it was measured again: from about 10:12 an unrelated program kept the CPU at 98–100 % and free memory below 10 GB, and the computer ran on battery for part of it; its results were equal but its times were not used. From then on every step waited for 2 minutes below 50 % CPU with at least 11000 MiB free before it started, and none of them saw CPU at 95 % or more or less than 10000 MiB free.",
